// REJECTS: Unexpected token '['. Valid alternatives: ['(']
//
// A point is PARENS `(x,y)`; a list of points is BRACKETS `[(x,y),(x,y)]`. Both appear in
// the same classView/propertyView block, three lines apart, meaning opposite things.
//
// Two coordinates in square brackets is what almost every other format uses for a point
// (GeoJSON, matplotlib, SVG path data in JSON form), so this is not a slip a reader
// catches. A rewrite that accepts either delimiter for a coordinate pair also has to
// decide what `points: [(1.0,2.0)]` means when the outer bracket is now ambiguous with a
// point -- so the permissiveness is not even locally contained.
###Diagram
Diagram fixture::neg::BracketPosition
{
   classView v1
   {
      class: fixture::neg::Person;
      position: [1.0,2.0];
      rectangle: (10.0,20.0);
   }
}
